
====================================================================================================
A0 -- a_i = D_i ln N (exact) and what it forces
====================================================================================================
  T=t, u_mu=-N delta^0_mu  =>  a_i = u^a grad_a u_i = D_i ln N.  IMPORTED-standard
  (khronometric/Horava, unitary gauge).  Consequence used throughout: at fixed N the
  covector a_i is metric-INDEPENDENT; all h-dependence of X is via h^ij and all
  h-dependence of T_ij is via Gamma^k_ij and h^ij.
  [ok  ] a_i = D_i ln N accepted (IMPORTED)

====================================================================================================
A -- delta_1 T_ij for a TT mode: the three operator identities, at GENERAL angle
====================================================================================================
  [ok  ] gamma traceless
  [ok  ] gamma transverse (d_i gamma_ij = 0) at general mu
  [ok  ] IDENTITY 1: delta^ij dGamma^z_ij = 0  => TF[dGamma^z]=dGamma^z
  [ok  ] IDENTITY 2: d_i d_j (dGamma^z_ij) = 0 IDENTICALLY for any TT gamma   -> annihilates the F_Y lapse-graviton cross term (no k^3 source)
  [ok  ] IDENTITY 3: d_j gamma_zj = 0 -> kills the O(a k) eta_K and F_X couplings
  [ok  ] TRANSVERSALITY THEOREM: <TF[d_i d_j phi] : dGamma^z_ij> = 0 at ALL angles
  [ok  ] <dT_ij dT^ij> = (1/4) a^2 k^2 (h+^2+hx^2) at GENERAL mu -- isotropic, +/x identical   got k**2*q**2*(hpc**2 + hxc**2)/4
  => ya_tensor_exact_2026.py section-F 'identically zero for k || a^(0)' is FALSE.
     [tensor-KT-GT] correction (iii) UPHELD.

====================================================================================================
B -- PURE TT BLOCK from the full ADM Lagrangian:  K_T and G_T
====================================================================================================
  TADPOLE RULE (same as the claims'): the background is NOT a solution, so terms
  proportional to the background field equations contaminate the k^0 (mass) sector.
  Those are k- and omega-INDEPENDENT, so ONLY the omega^2, k^2, k^4 coefficients are
  quoted.  (This is why the raw L2 below carries log(abar/(abar+q)) = F(X0) junk.)
  coef(omega^2) = (hpc**2 + hps**2 + hxc**2 + hxs**2)/4
  coef(k^2)     = -(hpc**2 + hps**2 + hxc**2 + hxs**2)*(abar**8 + 4*abar**6*q**2 + 6*abar**4*q**4 + 2*abar**2*epsilon*q**6 + 4*abar**2*q**6 + q**8)/(4*(abar**2 + q**2)**4)
  coef(k^4)     = 0
  coef(k^3)     = 0    coef(k^1) = 0
  [ok  ] NO k^4 and NO k^3 in the pure TT block
  [ok  ] K_T carries NO eps: K_T = 1 (normalised to GR)
  [ok  ] K_T free of lam_K and eta_K
  [ok  ] G_T = 1 + 2 eps A(X0) X0 EXACTLY   GT = (abar**8 + 4*abar**6*q**2 + 6*abar**4*q**4 + 2*abar**2*epsilon*q**6 + 4*abar**2*q**6 + q**8)/(abar**8 + 4*abar**6*q**2 + 6*abar**4*q**4 + 4*abar**2*q**6 + q**8)
  [ok  ] c_T^2/c^2 = G_T/K_T = 1 + 2 eps X0^3/(1+X0)^4   c_T^2 = (abar**8 + 4*abar**6*q**2 + 6*abar**4*q**4 + 2*abar**2*epsilon*q**6 + 4*abar**2*q**6 + q**8)/(abar**2 + q**2)**4
  [ok  ] c_T^2 ISOTROPIC in khat.ahat
  [ok  ] c_T^2 free of lam_K and eta_K in the pure TT block
  [ok  ] c_T^2 k-INDEPENDENT: no dispersion
  [ok  ] + and x give IDENTICAL omega^2 and k^2 coefficients (no birefringence in TT block)
  [max_X X^3/(1+X)^4 = 27/256 at X=3  =>  |c_T/c - 1| <= 0.10547|eps|]

====================================================================================================
C -- PRIORITY 1: is delta N sourced at LINEAR order in gamma^TT at finite a^(0)?
====================================================================================================
   d2L/dhpc dphic = q**2*(mu - 1)*(mu + 1)*(abar*eta_K + 2*abar + eta_K*q)/(2*(abar + q))
   d2L/dhpc dphis = -abar*k*mu*q**2*(mu - 1)*(mu + 1)/(abar + q)**2
   d2L/dhps dphic = abar*k*mu*q**2*(mu - 1)*(mu + 1)/(abar + q)**2
   d2L/dhps dphis = q**2*(mu - 1)*(mu + 1)*(abar*eta_K + 2*abar + eta_K*q)/(2*(abar + q))
  [ok  ] the x polarisation NEVER sources the lapse: coupling is pure '+'
  [ok  ] delta N IS sourced at LINEAR TT order for generic mu   ==> outcome (iii) of indirect_k4_criterion_2026.py is FALSE
  [ok  ] source VANISHES at exact alignment mu=1 (k || a^(0))   -> a run done only at k||a would wrongly report 'identically zero'

  in-phase  measured/predicted[-(eta_K-2F_X) a^2 (1-mu^2)] = 1/2
  out-phase measured/predicted[F_XX X0 a k mu (1-mu^2)]    = 2

  highest power of k, in-phase source : k^0
  highest power of k, out-of-phase    : k^1
  [ok  ] in-phase source carries NO derivatives (k^0)
  [ok  ] out-of-phase source carries EXACTLY ONE power of k -- no k^2, no k^3

